Z||000000||LottaBallsCamaro||01-30-2001||04:08 PM||||I just met a guy that swears his Z34 has 400hp!!! Its turbocharged and it has enough power to spin tires all the way up to 40mph. How can you make a3.4 withstand that much boost and is a 3.4 alumminum block? That would be a fast fu*king Fiero!||||reg||1
Z||000001||terryk||01-30-2001||04:17 PM||||First of all, I've never heard that GM made an aluminum DOHC block (they are substantially different from a pushrod block). Maybe they did but they DOHC people would be dreaming about it if they did.<P>Second, sure, 400HP is possible. It's all a matter of life. A top fueler will last about 2 minutes at full power and 5500HP so a 400HP DOHC is a piece of cake...for awhile.<P>Third, claims like that require a dyno sheet to support but it's certainly not out of the question.<P>IMBO<P>TK<P>||||reg||1
